# MuOffline — line-ending and content-type rules
#
# Why this file matters more than usual here: Phase 1's evidence model rests on
# hashes (PLAN_P1.md §4, §6). Platform-dependent line-ending translation would
# make a file's hash depend on which machine checked it out, which would silently
# invalidate provenance records. Everything below exists to make content
# byte-identical everywhere.

# Normalize text in the repository; check out LF so hashes are stable across
# Windows, WSL, and CI. Git still accepts CRLF from a Windows editor on commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Documentation and records — the entire tracked content today.
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary game assets — DO NOT relax these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Carried forward from the seed's own .gitattributes, which records the reason
# (MuMain issue #516): some encrypted .bmd / .oz* files contain no NUL bytes, so
# `text=auto` misdetects them as text. On a Windows checkout their lone LF is
# rewritten to CRLF, corrupting the file by exactly one byte — silently, and in
# a way that only surfaces later as a load failure or a wrong render.
#
# These rules are declared now, before any asset tree is tracked, so the
# protection is already in place when a working copy lands. Case-insensitive
# classes cover the mixed-case extensions used across the asset tree.
*.[Bb][Mm][Dd]     binary
*.[Oo][Zz][Bb]     binary
*.[Oo][Zz][Jj]     binary
*.[Oo][Zz][Jj]2    binary
*.[Oo][Zz][Tt]     binary
*.[Oo][Zz][Gg]     binary
*.[Oo][Zz][Pp]     binary
*.[Oo][Zz][Dd]     binary
*.[Aa][Tt][Tt]     binary
*.[Mm][Aa][Pp]     binary
*.[Oo][Bb][Jj]     binary
*.[Cc][Ww][Ss]     binary
*.[Cc][Ss][Rr]     binary
*.[Tt][Gg][Aa]     binary
*.[Bb][Mm][Pp]     binary
*.[Jj][Pp][Gg]     binary
*.[Jj][Pp][Ee][Gg] binary
*.[Pp][Nn][Gg]     binary
*.[Ww][Aa][Vv]     binary
*.[Oo][Gg][Gg]     binary
*.[Mm][Pp]3        binary

# Captured evidence artifacts (traces, packet captures, screenshots, video)
# are never text and must never be normalized.
*.pcap  binary
*.pcapng binary
*.bin   binary
*.trace binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary
